# width: 120
# height: 40
# Twelve buffers at 120 columns overflow the strip, and the strip says
# so whatever its window: the pager ` ‹ n/m › ` (`ui/stepper.zig`) —
# the page on show, of how many — and after it the ` ⋯ ` that opens the
# buffer picker. It once took a ` +N hidden ` count chip, painted only
# when the window happened to leave it room, so twelve buffers said
# nothing about the missing ones; nothing is hidden now (every page is
# a click away), so no count is painted at all.
write file01name.txt x
write file02name.txt x
write file03name.txt x
write file04name.txt x
write file05name.txt x
write file06name.txt x
write file07name.txt x
write file08name.txt x
write file09name.txt x
write file10name.txt x
write file11name.txt x
write file12name.txt x
open file01name.txt
open file02name.txt
open file03name.txt
open file04name.txt
open file05name.txt
open file06name.txt
open file07name.txt
open file08name.txt
open file09name.txt
open file10name.txt
open file11name.txt
open file12name.txt
expect screen contains "file12name.txt"
expect screen contains "file12name.txt 󰅖   󰐕"
expect screen contains "‹ 6/6 ›  ⋯"
expect screen lacks "hidden"
